WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:08.340
Wormable prompt injection is not just a stronger phrase for ordinary prompt
injection. It describes a propagation risk in connected AI systems.

2
00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:20.500
A model sees untrusted content, treats part of that content as instruction,
and then helps move the influence into another system, user workflow, memory
store, retrieval corpus, connector, or agent.

3
00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:27.300
The important feature is not clever wording. The important feature is an
application path that lets malicious influence travel.

4
00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:36.180
The Morris-II research made this risk concrete. It studied adversarial
self-replicating prompts in GenAI ecosystems that use retrieval-augmented
generation.

5
00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:42.740
The paper describes a computer-worm-like chain reaction where a prompt can
trigger indirect prompt injections across connected applications.

6
00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:51.140
That research is a warning about architecture, not an invitation to build
payloads. In this course, we discuss the mechanics only at a defensive
level.

7
00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:56.420
Wormability requires several conditions. There must be untrusted content
that an AI system processes.

8
00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:03.060
There must be enough authority for the system to produce output, take
action, update memory, or write to a shared surface.

9
00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:07.380
There must be a path by which that output reaches another model-enabled
workflow.

10
00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:13.140
And there must be weak enough trust boundaries that the downstream system
may treat the propagated content as instruction.

11
00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:16.420
That means the risk lives outside the model as much as inside it.

12
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:31.860
Email assistants, shared document summarizers, RAG systems, ticket triage
tools, browser agents, chat connectors, and workflow automations can all
create spread paths if they copy, summarize, forward, store, or act on
untrusted text without strong controls.

13
00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:41.380
The defensive goal is to break the chain. A system should assume that
retrieved documents, tool results, emails, comments, and web pages may
contain hostile instructions.

14
00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:49.540
The application must keep data separate from authority, restrict actions,
preserve provenance, and prevent untrusted content from becoming a command
channel.
